# What Delphi actually depends on, and nothing else.
#
# This file is the intent; requirements.txt is the consequence. Compile it with
#
#     uv pip compile --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 \
#         requirements.in -o requirements.txt
#
# which resolves these into every package that really gets installed — the ones
# named here and the two dozen they pull in behind them — each at one exact
# version, each with the hash of the file it must be. The Dockerfile and CI
# then install with --require-hashes, so a build either gets precisely that or
# stops.
#
# 3.12 is the image's Python (see Dockerfile). Resolving for the interpreter
# that happens to be handy would pin whatever *it* needs, and markers differ
# between versions.
#
# Bounds here are the range Delphi is written against. They are not what gets
# installed — that is the lock file — they are the range Dependabot is allowed
# to move within when it opens an update.

